1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,600
You can deploy Burp Suite Enterprise Edition either to a single machine or multiple machines.

2
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:15,120
For a single machine deployment, this means you can run all components on a single physical or

3
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:21,040
virtual machine, which includes the bundled database. This option is suitable for a trial

4
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:26,640
or evaluation, but for production deployments we recommend that you connect to an external database

5
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:32,880
and use a multi-machine deployment. We can see from the diagram that all Burp Suite Enterprise Edition

6
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:40,160
components have been installed to a single physical or virtual machine. This makes setup and installation

7
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:44,000
very straightforward, but does limit the number of concurrent scans that we can run.

8
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:52,960
Alternatively, you can run scans on several different machines and you can use your own

9
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:58,080
external database for storage. This option lets you scale the number of concurrent scans that you

10
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:03,200
could potentially run to be indefinitely large and utilize any existing database infrastructure that

11
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:08,480
you have. We can see from the diagram that the components have been separated out to their own

12
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:14,880
physical or virtual machines, which gives greater scale and performance. Please note that the Enterprise

13
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:21,120
Server and Web Server are always deployed to a single machine. For specific details about the system

14
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:38,240
requirements for both of these options, please refer to the system requirements page. Thank you.

